# Rivet — HOSTED environment template (Vercel + Supabase Cloud)
#
# This is NOT a file you copy to disk. It is the checklist of variables to paste
# into the Vercel dashboard. Local development uses .env.example instead — the
# values there are localhost defaults and none of them belong in production.
#
# Source of truth for every value below is the shared 1Password vault. Fill the
# vault first, then paste into the dashboards. Nothing here should ever be
# committed with a real value, and nothing should sit in a .env file on a laptop.
#
#   docs/PROTOTYPE_DEPLOYMENT.md   the deploy runbook these values feed
#   docs/adr/0005-...              why Vercel + Supabase
#   docs/adr/0009-...              why there is no separate AI service
#
# ROTATE BEFORE FIRST USE. Every key that exists today has lived in a
# tunnel-facing dev config and been copied between machines during the laptop
# migration. Treat all of them as exposed — docs/LAUNCH_PLAN.md, P0.


# =============================================================================
# VERCEL  —  Project → Settings → Environment Variables
# =============================================================================
# Scope to Production + Preview. Preview deploys share the staging database, so
# do not point Preview at production once a production project exists.

# ─── Supabase (auth only — application data goes through DATABASE_URL) ────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<Supabase → Settings → API → anon/publishable>
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<Supabase → Settings → API → service_role/secret>

# Only needed if the AI service moves to real JWT verification.
# SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=<Supabase → Settings → API → JWT secret>

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Read directly by src/lib/db/index.ts and NOT covered by the Zod schema in
# src/lib/env.ts — a typo here fails at query time with a connection error
# rather than loudly at boot. Check it twice.
#
# MUST be the TRANSACTION-MODE POOLER on port 6543, never the direct 5432
# connection. The pool is max:5 per instance and Vercel multiplies that by
# concurrency; the direct connection will exhaust under trivial load.
# Supabase → Settings → Database → Connection string → Transaction pooler.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<project-ref>:<db-password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# ─── App URL ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public quote and invoice links are built from this. Wrong value = links that
# point at the wrong host in real customer email.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://<your-app>.vercel.app

# ─── AI (Gemini) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Google models only — a standing decision, see CLAUDE.md.
#
# Gemini is called in-process from the server actions; there is no second
# service, no shared secret and no backend URL (docs/adr/0009-ai-in-process.md).
# Server-side only — this key must never reach the browser bundle, so it has no
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and must not be given one.
GEMINI_API_KEY=<rotated key>

# Optional. Tried in order; unset uses the default in src/lib/ai/gemini.ts.
# Note gemini-2.5-flash now 404s for newly issued keys.
# GEMINI_MODELS=gemini-flash-latest,gemini-2.5-flash,gemini-flash-lite-latest

# ─── Email (Resend) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without SPF/DKIM/DMARC on the sending domain, quote email lands in spam and
# the product silently does not work. docs/LAUNCH_PLAN.md, P1.
RESEND_API_KEY=<rotated key>
RESEND_FROM_EMAIL=no-reply@<your-domain>

# ─── Payments (Stripe) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keep TEST mode until Rivet's own billing exists. Live mode is P1.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_<...>
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_<...>
STRIPE_PLATFORM_FEE_BPS=0

# ─── E-signature ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Without it the quote viewer falls back to instant acceptance.
# DROPBOX_SIGN_API_KEY=<rotated key>

# ─── Observability (config files exist, packages not installed yet) ──────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# ─── Not wired — do not set ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID / TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN   SMS. Needs TCPA consent capture
#                                          before it ships — see
#                                          docs/GTM_BUSINESS_CHECKLIST.md 4.1.
# LEMONSQUEEZY_API_KEY                     Rivet's own billing, does not exist.


# =============================================================================
# AFTER DEPLOY — verify, don't assume
# =============================================================================
# Generate a quote in the app and check `mode` on the result.
#     -> "gemini:<model>". "mock" means quotes are keyword-matched from the
#        catalog rather than generated, which fails silently. Alert on it.
#        The usual cause is a missing or empty GEMINI_API_KEY.
#
# Check the function logs for `ai/quote: dropped items with no catalog match`.
#     -> Each one is a line item the model invented that was discarded before
#        it reached a customer. A steady stream means the catalog is missing
#        something the contractor actually sells.
#
# Vercel → Deployment Protection → Vercel Authentication (Standard) is ON.
#     That is the entire access-control story for an internal prototype.
